<task id="075" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author /provision-environment operator skill (L3) per §4.3a — 15-tool matrix + prereqs + intake + gate + execute loop + handoff report</title>
    <phase>D L3 Skill + BFF Integration Endpoints + Metering</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New file creation without BFF touch — a skill directive, not code. Per project CLAUDE.md rigor defaults + root CLAUDE.md §8 STANDARD row. Note: Sub-Agent Write Boundary forces parallel-safe:false.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Skill authoring covering 15-tool matrix + fallback matrix + interactive intake + gate/execute loop is a design-heavy operator-UX task — high-blast-radius because it becomes THE mechanism for every provisioning going forward. Step 3.5.5b Opus tier justified (architectural/skill-directive scope).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Writes to .claude/skills/** — Sub-Agent Write Boundary per root CLAUDE.md §3 forces MAIN-SESSION-ONLY; sub-agents will fail with "Edit denied on .claude/...". task-create Step 3.8 auto-marks these.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>057, 042</deps>
    <tags>skill-directive, l2-controlplane, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Author the /provision-environment operator skill at .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md per spec.md FR-25 + §4.3a. The skill Step 0 is a prerequisites check (pwsh ≥ 7.4, az ≥ 2.60, pac ≥ 1.35, git ≥ 2.40, operator az login succeeded, L2 API reachable, Dataverse MCP status optional). Interactive intake collects customerId / tenantId / tenancyModel / profile. Preflight → confirmation gate → execute loop (enqueue via L2 REST → poll GET /api/runs/{id} → advance on manual gates surfacing actionable instructions) → completion writes handoff report to runs/{runId}.md + updates sprk_dataverseenvironment via Dataverse MCP + produces final summary. Reference model: .claude/skills/deploy-new-release/SKILL.md.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform skill author. Fluent with the Claude Code skill format (.claude/skills/{name}/SKILL.md), the 15-tool operator-toolchain matrix per §4.3a, interactive-intake + confirmation-gate patterns from /deploy-new-release, and the L2 REST API surface from task 057. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md exists as an operator skill; describes Step 0 prereqs, interactive intake, preflight-then-confirm gate, execute loop against L2 REST, manual-gate handling with actionable instructions, completion handoff report at runs/{runId}.md + sprk_dataverseenvironment update via Dataverse MCP. Skill is invocable via /provision-environment. Dry-run mode supported.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-25 + §4.3a + design.md §4.3a.4: the L3 skill is the operator's entry point to the entire provisioning platform. Today (Gen 1) operators merge 3 docs by hand + invoke scripts sequentially. The skill wraps L2's REST surface (task 057) into a guided flow with prereq checks, an intake wizard, a confirmation gate before execution, and a poll loop that surfaces manual gates (customer admin consent, Azure quota bumps, SPE cert bootstrap) with actionable instructions. Reference model /deploy-new-release exists as a strong template.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/skills/deploy-new-release/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Api/RunsEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="057" status="pending">L2 REST endpoints — the surface the skill invokes</dependency>
      <dependency task="042" status="pending">H0.5 consent-callback BFF endpoint — referenced by the skill for Model 2 flows</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-25">SCOPE: Step 0 prereqs check (pwsh ≥ 7.4, az ≥ 2.60, pac ≥ 1.35, git ≥ 2.40, operator az login, L2 API reachable, MCP status optional); intake collects customerId/tenantId/tenancyModel/profile; preflight → confirmation gate → execute loop → completion handoff report.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4.3a">SCOPE: 15-tool matrix per §4.3a — pwsh, bash, WebFetch, az, pac, Dataverse MCP, Azure MCP (with fallbacks); operator's OWN AAD identity (not SP) per NFR-11.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§3">SCOPE: This skill file writes to .claude/skills/** — MAIN-SESSION-ONLY per Sub-Agent Write Boundary; parallel-safe:false enforced by task-create Step 3.8.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§11">SCOPE: NEW-surface task — justification field completed per §11 three-question gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Skill produces a handoff report at runs/{runId}.md in the operator's working directory; NOT under .claude/ (runs are per-operator-invocation, not repo state).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Skill uses Dataverse MCP for the sprk_dataverseenvironment update; MCP-unreachable triggers fallback matrix per FR-25 (task 076 authors fallback impl).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Confirmation gate at design.md §4.3a.4 semantics — user MUST type an explicit "proceed" phrase; a bare "y" is insufficient.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§6.5">SCOPE: Auditable operator action per NFR-11 — every mutating L2 call the skill makes carries the operator's actor tid; the L2 side audit-logs (task 061).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>L3 /provision-environment skill authoring — reference /deploy-new-release + spec §4.3a</topic>
    <files>
