      <file>CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Skill format" location=".claude/skills/deploy-new-release/SKILL.md">Existing operator skill with pre-flight, confirmation gate, script execution, and release-tag steps; copy structure.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (STANDARD, main-session-only). Load spec.md FR-25 + §4.3a + design.md §4.3a.4 + /deploy-new-release SKILL.md.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Outline">Draft skill outline: Trigger phrases, Step 0 prereqs, Step 1 intake, Step 2 preflight, Step 3 confirmation gate, Step 4 execute loop, Step 5 manual-gate handling, Step 6 completion handoff.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Write skill">Author .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md with all 6+ steps + tool matrix + confirmation-gate phrase requirement + handoff-report template.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Tool matrix">Document the 15-tool matrix per §4.3a with fallback references (task 076 owns fallback impl).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Test dry-run">Manually walk through the skill in a dry-run against dev L2 (no actual provisioning); verify each step produces expected output.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Cross-reference">Add pointer row to root CLAUDE.md §17 Pointers table linking the new skill and cross-reference from project CLAUDE.md.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 075 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: .claude/skills/deploy-new-release/SKILL.md (release-deploy skill, different lifecycle stage). Grep for `provision-environment` under .claude/skills/ returns none.</existing>
    <extension>No — provisioning has different phases (H0..H14 handler catalog), different gates (Model 2 admin consent, Azure quota, SPE 24h), different error semantics (§4C 4-class taxonomy), different auth flow (operator's own AAD per §4.3a.2). Extending /deploy-new-release would violate its single-purpose contract per spec.md § New Components table row 3.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without L3 skill, operator invokes L2 REST manually via curl/az rest + tracks 19-handler state by hand + loses fallback matrix for MCP disconnects (§4.3a.5). Spec.md § New Components table row 3 explicitly cites this failure mode. The skill is HOW the operator uses L2 at all — without it, L2 is inaccessible except to engineers reading OpenAPI.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Test-invoke the skill via manual walk-through</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md</output>
    <output type="docs">CLAUDE.md (pointer row added)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md (cross-reference)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md exists with Step 0 prereqs, intake, preflight, confirmation gate, execute loop, and completion handoff sections.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 0 lists all 6 prerequisite checks per FR-25: pwsh ≥ 7.4, az ≥ 2.60, pac ≥ 1.35, git ≥ 2.40, operator az login, L2 API reachable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Confirmation gate requires an explicit "proceed" phrase (not a bare "y") per §4.3a.4.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Skill invokes L2 REST endpoints (task 057) and polls GET /api/runs/{id} for progress; surfaces manual gates with actionable instructions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Completion produces a handoff report at runs/{runId}.md in the operator's cwd (NOT under .claude/).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Skill updates sprk_dataverseenvironment via Dataverse MCP; MCP-unreachable triggers fallback per task 076.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Root CLAUDE.md §17 Pointers table has a row linking the skill.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Manual dry-run against dev L2 walks all steps without runtime error.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-25 + §4.3a + NFR-11 + design.md §4.3a.4. Companion: task 076 (fallback matrix).</notes>

